{"pagination":{"maxPageableSet":"10000","numFound":2,"query":"name=Klinkenborg&limit=10&title=Several Short Sentences About Writing","limit":10,"start":0},"items":{"mods":[{"titleInfo":{"title":"Several short sentences about writing"},"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Klinkenborg, Verlyn","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"Alfred A. Knopf","dateIssued":"2012","edition":"1st ed.","issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"203 p. ; 21 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"A widely admired writer and teacher of writing, Verlyn Klinkenborg now gives us a distillation of that experience in an distinctive book that will help anyone who wants to write, write better, or have a clearer understanding of what it means for them to be writing. Klinkenborg believes that most of our received wisdom about how writing works is not only wrong but an obstacle to our ability to write. Here he sets out to help us unlearn that \"wisdom\"--about genius, about creativity, about writer's block, topic sentences, and outline--and understand that writing is just as much about thinking, noticing, and learning what it means to be involved in the act of writing. There is no gospel, no orthodoxy, no dogma in this book. Instead, it is a gathering of starting points in a journey toward lively, lucid, satisfying self-expression.--From publisher description."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Verlyn Klinkenborg."},"\"This is a Borzoi Book.\""],"sub